<figure class="decision-figure capability-flow" id="engineering-capability-flow" aria-labelledby="capability-flow-title">
  <h3 id="capability-flow-title">Exploration and delivery strengthen each other</h3>
  <p class="figure-intro">Begin with enough information to investigate the next question. Promote only the learning that needs to guide later work.</p>

  <section class="flow-loop" aria-labelledby="exploration-loop-title">
    <h4 id="exploration-loop-title">Explore the next question</h4>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Partial intent</strong><span>Needs, constraints and open questions</span></li>
      <li><strong>Agent-supported model or prototype</strong><span>A disposable artifact for a selected question</span></li>
      <li><strong>Feedback sharpens the question</strong><span>Expose assumptions and decide what deserves deeper engineering</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <p class="promotion"><strong>Promote selected learning — not every prototype</strong></p>

  <section class="flow-loop delivery-loop" aria-labelledby="delivery-loop-title">
    <h4 id="delivery-loop-title">Make the change deliverable</h4>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Versioned definitions</strong><span>Intent, interfaces and acceptance criteria</span></li>
      <li><strong>Bounded agent work</strong><span>Permitted tools, independent checks and review</span></li>
      <li><strong>Integrated release candidate</strong><span>The identified product and support material that belong together</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <p class="return-path"><strong>Integration and use create new questions</strong> that can return the team to exploration.</p>
  <figcaption>Exploration and delivery are concurrent feedback loops. Early artifacts expose uncertainty; selected learning becomes maintained engineering information, checks and release capability.</figcaption>
</figure>

